  "body": {
    "id": "thm:sharp-rounding-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "The sharp same-size realization frontier has rate \\(r_N=N^{-1}\\): for every \\(N\\ge4\\), \\(1/(46080N)\\le\\Delta_N\\le\\min\\{1/4,402/N\\}\\).  There is no arithmetic exceptional subsequence for this asymptotic order.  Moreover, \\(\\Delta_2=0\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "N",
      "\\Delta_N"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:worst-gap",
      "thm:fixed-contrast-support-dichotomy",
      "thm:constructive-rounding-upper",
      "thm:explicit-matching-lower"
    ],
    "justification": "The original three-arm frontier is now a corollary of the scalar fixed-contrast support-size dichotomy; the affine transfer additionally yields the stronger incidental lower constant \\(5/215296\\).",
    "gap": "Gao, Ge, and Qian (2025) target the fractional multi-marginal optimum, while the closest empirical Monge papers establish existence or counterexamples without a same-size minimax rate.",
    "consumer": "The corollary preserves the finite-population causal application while the general theorem explains why the phase transition occurs exactly at three active coefficients.",
    "proof_tex": "Apply Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm{:}fixed\\mbox{-}contrast\\mbox{-}support\\mbox{-}dichotomy}\\) with \\(K=3\\) and \\(\\widetilde c=(1/4,1/4,-1/2)\\).  Equations (25)--(26) give, for every \\(N\\ge4\\),\n\\[\n \\frac{5}{215296N}\\le\\Delta_N<\\frac{402}{N}. \\tag{40}\n\\]\nSince \\(5\\cdot46080=230400>215296\\), the lower bound in (40) implies \\(\\Delta_N\\ge1/(46080N)\\).  The direct cost range gives \\(\\Delta_N\\le1/4\\), proving the frozen two-sided display.  The stronger lower bound holds for every \\(N\\ge4\\), so in particular there is no arithmetic exceptional subsequence.  Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm{:}explicit\\mbox{-}matching\\mbox{-}lower}\\) independently realizes the frozen stated constant exactly on its original padded family.\n\nFor \\(N=2\\), write the two scaled values in arm \\(a\\) as \\(m_a-d_a\\) and \\(m_a+d_a\\), with \\(d_a\\ge0\\).  Any fractional coupling is a law of \\(S\\in\\{-1,1\\}^3\\) with \\(\\mathbb ES_a=0\\); when \\(d_a=0\\), an auxiliary balanced sign label leaves the values unchanged.  With \\(M=\\sum_am_a\\),\n\\[\n \\mathbb E\\left(M+\\sum_ad_aS_a\\right)^2\n =M^2+\\mathbb E\\left(\\sum_ad_aS_a\\right)^2. \\tag{41}\n\\]\nAntipodal symmetrization preserves balanced marginals and (41).  Every antipodally symmetric law is a convex combination of the four laws uniform on a pair \\(\\{s,-s\\}\\).  Because (41) is linear in that law, one pair law attains the fractional minimum.  It is exactly a two-row schedule using each marginal occurrence once.  Thus \\(V_{\\mathrm{int}}(F)=V_{\\mathrm{rel}}(F)\\) for every two-row triple and \\(\\Delta_2=0\\).",
